    {
      "id": "qqs9fvy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Difference Between Plant Cell and Animal Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Mitochondria are known as the 'Powerhouse of the Cell' due to ATP generation during cellular respiration.",
        "Lysosomes are designated as 'Suicidal Bags' because they contain hydrolytic enzymes capable of digesting cellular waste.",
        "Ribosomes are non-membrane-bound organelles responsible for protein synthesis in both prokaryotes and eukaryotes.",
        "Plant cell walls are primarily composed of cellulose, whereas fungal cell walls are made of chitin."
      ],
      "id": "nze5poo"
    },
